         <ieeecs:Author1SName>Maiden</ieeecs:Author1SName>
         <ieeecs:Author1FName>Neil</ieeecs:Author1FName>
         <ieeecs:ArticleTitle>The Inhibited Analyst</ieeecs:ArticleTitle>
         <ieeecs:Abstract>Requirements analysts need to ask the right questions repeatedly. They need to be more inquisitive and know why people want things as well as what happens beforehand. This requires them to become less inhibited and keep asking questions until they and their stakeholders are satisfied with the answers.</ieeecs:Abstract>
